behavior, rather than ethics,

01:05:36.835 --> 01:05:40.060
that could be driven by
the fact that behaviors

01:05:40.060 --> 01:05:43.910
might be easier to measure than attitudes.

01:05:43.910 --> 01:05:45.210
And so I, A,

01:05:45.210 --> 01:05:47.160
I would definitely encourage you

01:05:47.160 --> 01:05:50.220
to explore more effective ways to extract

01:05:50.220 --> 01:05:52.610
this information from the
data, like (indistinct).

01:05:52.610 --> 01:05:54.230
- Can I put this question back to you,

01:05:54.230 --> 01:05:56.350
'cause this is something I've
been thinking a lot about.

01:05:56.350 --> 01:05:58.920
Can we ever definitively
answer the question,

01:05:58.920 --> 01:06:01.540
are behaviors easier
to move than attitudes?

01:06:01.540 --> 01:06:04.140
Given that you can't put them on the same,

01:06:04.140 --> 01:06:06.580
it's impossible to standardize,
it's a serious question,

01:06:06.580 --> 01:06:09.020
'cause it's such a prevalent thing.

01:06:09.020 --> 01:06:11.039
- [Lushvig] Well, the
second part of my question

01:06:11.039 --> 01:06:13.540
was going partly in that direction.

01:06:13.540 --> 01:06:14.680
So, one possibility,

01:06:14.680 --> 01:06:17.921
especially given your context should be,

01:06:17.921 --> 01:06:22.921
I wouldn't say easy but feasible

01:06:23.020 --> 01:06:27.820
is to try to design some
alternative measures based

01:06:27.820 --> 01:06:31.983
